# Environment for GLM-OCR Hungarian post-training on a rented CUDA box.
# Unpinned intent; `requirements.txt` next to this file is the compiled lock.
# Recompile with:  make lock
#
# One environment holds BOTH the trainer and the inference server. That is only
# possible inside a narrow window, so the three pins below are load-bearing:
#
#   LLaMA-Factory 100e9a4 requires  transformers >=4.55.0,<=5.8.0,!=5.6.0
#   vllm 0.28.0           requires  transformers >=5.5.3        + torch ==2.13.0
#   vllm 0.29.0           requires  transformers >=5.10.4       <- NO OVERLAP
#
# So 0.28.0 is the newest vllm that can share a venv with this trainer.
# Bumping vllm past it forces a second venv and a second ~3 GB torch stack.
# transformers 5.8.0 is also the version verified to carry `glm_ocr` in
# CONFIG_MAPPING_NAMES; the build asserts it rather than trusting this comment.

torch==2.13.0
vllm==0.28.0
transformers<=5.8.0

# The trainer, pinned by commit -- the revision verified end to end on macOS
# 2026-09-13 (LLaMA-Factory 0.9.6.dev0). A moving `main` here would mean the
# image that produced a checkpoint is unreproducible.
llamafactory @ git+https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory.git@100e9a4

# LLaMA-Factory's requirements/metrics.txt -- it computes BLEU/ROUGE during eval
# and dies at eval time, not import time, without these.
nltk
jieba
rouge-chinese

# ocr-post-training's own runtime deps, so the private repo installs on the box
# with `pip install -e . --no-deps` -- zero resolution against the clock.
typer
pydantic
pydantic-settings
rich
pillow
pymupdf
fonttools
numpy

# No [cli] extra: hub 1.x ships the `hf` command in the base package, and asking
# for the extra is only a warning, not an error -- easy to leave in and believe.
huggingface-hub
